{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:UGB.UnitalGroebner.generator_choice","@type":"LeanModule","name":"UGB.UnitalGroebner.generator_choice","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Basic"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.UnitalGroebner.generator_choice","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.UnitalGroebner.generator_choice","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/UnitalGroebner/generator_choice.lean#L50-L75","doc":"**Generator choice — single division step.**\n\nWhenever the division algorithm performs a reduction step\n`f → g` (a `SingleStepReduction`), that step is realised by an\nactual rule `r ∈ sys.rules` — the chosen generator `g_γ ∈ G` —\nwhose leading monomial occurs as a subword of some monomial in the\nsupport of `f`. This is precisely \"we may take `hᵢ = g_{γᵢ}`\".\n\nThe conclusion is a **concrete nested existential** over\n`ReductionRule`/`Monomial` (membership in `sys.rules`, an `isInfix`\noccurrence), not a bare `Prop`. Proved directly from the reduction\nwitness. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:generator-choice","label":"lem:generator-choice","md":"unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/generator-choice-lemma.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}